 "decision": "Not shipped. The audit shows the lost-frame error is not confined to the tracked outlines: her Q48 thigh muscles (transferred onto her CT bones, then refined to photographed septa in the SAME lost frame) sit shifted in the same direction (best muscle fit up to ~10 mm on the left). Registering the outlines to her femur therefore leaves 8-13 mm of muscle mesh over them (sciatic 32,019 of 46,907 full-res vertices > 1 mm inside, max 13.3 mm; femoral a/v in pectineus max 9.6/9.2 mm, worse than shipped), and the bounded Q177 face snap removes little (all < 1.4 % volume, but e.g. biceps femoris_l 15,595 -> 13,103 vertices, max 13.3 -> 10.5 mm; pectineus_r 4,026 -> 3,853): the fold guard and the 8 mm / 45 % caps bind. Needs an owner decision: (a) register her Q48 thigh muscles with the same per-level translation (touches Q48 geometry), (b) ship the registered outlines anyway with the larger disclosed overlap, or (c) keep the old frame for both and only clip in it (reconstructed old-frame shift is in vhf_tracked_reg_q179.json)."
}